            "review_title": "Review at Com Dong Nhan",
            "review_text": "dragon789wv\nAgoura Hills, California5397 contributions\n0\nHole in the wall, but pretty good\nMar 2013 • Friends\nWe were on a tour. Restaurant is reasonably close to the Oscar Saigon Hotel, but best to ask concierge where it is, as it might be difficult to find -- BUT well worth it! Small family restaurant, like many in Vietnam, serves all-around good food at very reasonable prices. We went back twice with 4 others from our tour, all of us Asians that have travelled extensively.\nBecause TripAdvisor had to verify and evaluate the restaurant, which took 6 months, I cannot remember what we had to eat, but it was all good. Sorry! I have made a suggestion to TripAdvisor that it would be best that they capture all the information, as if we were doing an actual evaluation, save the data, and then when it IS accepted, then they have all the information. To date, TripAdvisor has not accepted or implemented this suggestion. This is not the first one that wasn't on their list, unfortunately, but this one did take the longest before it was accepted.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 5, 2013",
